meta {
  name: 06_UnitHierarchyDelegationDirections
  seq: 6
}

docs {
  Scenario: Delegations between main units, subunits and persons show up for the receiving side

    Given a set of main units, their subunits and persons that have delegated to each other
    When a service owner looks up the receiving side as the subject
    Then the delegating party is in the subject's list with the access it delegated
    And access delegated by a main unit extends to that main unit's subunit

  The subject in the request body is always the RECEIVER of the delegation, either the person
  who received it directly or the daily leader of the receiving organisation, and the assertion
  is that the DELEGATOR appears. The directions covered here are main unit to main unit, main
  unit to person, person to main unit, person to person, person to subunit, subunit to main unit,
  main unit to subunit and subunit to subunit.

  The last two, main unit to subunit and subunit to subunit, were switched off in the folder this
  replaces with a skipScenario flag and an early return, so they registered no assertions and
  always passed. They are written for real here.
}
